    claim 1 is for the TTFT device.
    the HCPCS code of the TTFT device is "E0766".
    the TTFT device is furnished to Cy.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the WHO grade of the histologically confirmed astrocytoma of Cy is 4.
    the glioblastoma of Cy is newly diagnosed.
    the glioblastoma of Cy is supratentorial.
    Cy had maximal debulking surgery of the glioblastoma.
    the last dose of concomitant chemotherapy of Cy was on 2026-03-20.
    the last dose of concomitant radiotherapy of Cy was on 2026-03-25.
    the finding disease progression absent about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the Karnofsky performance score of Cy is 60.
    the finding full daily use expected about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the TTFT device was delivered on 2026-04-20.
    claim 2 is for the other TTFT device.
    the HCPCS code of the other TTFT device is "E0766".
    the other TTFT device is furnished to Dee.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 1.
    the WHO grade of the histologically confirmed astrocytoma of Dee is 4.
    the glioblastoma of Dee is supratentorial.
    Dee had maximal debulking surgery of the glioblastoma.
    the last dose of concomitant chemotherapy of Dee was on 2026-03-20.
    the last dose of concomitant radiotherapy of Dee was on 2026-03-25.
    the finding disease progression absent about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the Karnofsky performance score of Dee is 90.
    the finding full daily use expected about Dee is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the other TTFT device was delivered on 2026-04-20.
    rn expects answers [].

% Month 4: re-evaluated on day 75 with an average use of 20 hours a day
% (claim 1); the same for a beneficiary averaging 14 hours (claim 2).
scenario month_four_adherence is:
    claim 1 is for the TTFT device.
    the HCPCS code of the TTFT device is "E0766".
    the TTFT device is furnished to Eve.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-07-20.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    the WHO grade of the histologically confirmed astrocytoma of Eve is 4.
    the glioblastoma of Eve is newly diagnosed.
    the glioblastoma of Eve is supratentorial.
    Eve had maximal debulking surgery of the glioblastoma.
    the last dose of concomitant chemotherapy of Eve was on 2026-03-20.
    the last dose of concomitant radiotherapy of Eve was on 2026-03-25.
    the finding disease progression absent about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the Karnofsky performance score of Eve is 80.
    the finding full daily use expected about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the TTFT device was delivered on 2026-04-20.
    Eve had an in person clinical reevaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-07-04.
    the average daily use of the TTFT device in the usage data reviewed by the treating practitioner is 20 hours.
    claim 2 is for the other TTFT device.
    the HCPCS code of the other TTFT device is "E0766".
    the other TTFT device is furnished to Fay.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-07-20.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 4.
    the WHO grade of the histologically confirmed astrocytoma of Fay is 4.
    the glioblastoma of Fay is newly diagnosed.
    the glioblastoma of Fay is supratentorial.
    Fay had maximal debulking surgery of the glioblastoma.
    the last dose of concomitant chemotherapy of Fay was on 2026-03-20.
    the last dose of concomitant radiotherapy of Fay was on 2026-03-25.
    the finding disease progression absent about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the Karnofsky performance score of Fay is 80.
    the finding full daily use expected about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the other TTFT device was delivered on 2026-04-20.
    Fay had an in person clinical reevaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-07-04.
    the average daily use of the other TTFT device in the usage data reviewed by the treating practitioner is 14 hours.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A late re-evaluation (day 120, 18 August): the July claim is not covered,
% the September claim is.
scenario late_reevaluation is:
    claim 1 is for the TTFT device.
    the HCPCS code of the TTFT device is "E0766".
    the TTFT device is furnished to Gus.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-07-20.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 4.
    claim 2 is for the TTFT device.
    the date of service of claim 2 is 2026-09-20.
    the rental month of claim 2 is 6.
    the WHO grade of the histologically confirmed astrocytoma of Gus is 4.
    the glioblastoma of Gus is newly diagnosed.
    the glioblastoma of Gus is supratentorial.
    Gus had maximal debulking surgery of the glioblastoma.
    the last dose of concomitant chemotherapy of Gus was on 2026-03-20.
    the last dose of concomitant radiotherapy of Gus was on 2026-03-25.
    the finding disease progression absent about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the Karnofsky performance score of Gus is 80.
    the finding full daily use expected about Gus is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the TTFT device was delivered on 2026-04-20.
    Gus had an in person clinical reevaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-08-18.
    the average daily use of the TTFT device in the usage data reviewed by the treating practitioner is 19 hours.
    rn expects answers ["claim 2 is reasonable and necessary"].

% A beneficiary who began TTFT under another payer and enrolled in
% fee-for-service Medicare: evaluated after the enrollment, adherent,
% benefiting.
scenario entering_medicare is:
    claim 1 is for the TTFT device.
    the HCPCS code of the TTFT device is "E0766".
    the TTFT device is furnished to Hal.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    Hal was receiving tumor treatment field therapy before enrolling in fee for service Medicare.
    Hal enrolled in fee for service Medicare on 2026-06-01.
    the WHO grade of the histologically confirmed astrocytoma of Hal is 4.
    the glioblastoma of Hal is newly diagnosed.
    the glioblastoma of Hal is supratentorial.
    Hal had maximal debulking surgery of the glioblastoma.
    the last dose of concomitant chemotherapy of Hal was on 2025-11-10.
    the last dose of concomitant radiotherapy of Hal was on 2025-11-10.
    Hal had an in person clinical reevaluation by the treating practitioner on 2026-06-15.
    the average daily use of the TTFT device in the usage data reviewed by the treating practitioner is 21 hours.
    the finding deriving benefit from therapy about Hal is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].

% The Council finds the record does not show the absence of progression:
% the MRI before the start of therapy is read as progressive disease.
scenario council_progression_unsupported is:
    claim 1 is for the TTFT device.
    the HCPCS code of the TTFT device is "E0766".
    the TTFT device is furnished to Ida.
    the rental month of claim 1 is 1.
    the WHO grade of the histologically confirmed astrocytoma of Ida is 4.
    the glioblastoma of Ida is newly diagnosed.
    the glioblastoma of Ida is supratentorial.
    Ida had maximal debulking surgery of the glioblastoma.
    the last dose of concomitant chemotherapy of Ida was on 2026-03-20.
    the last dose of concomitant radiotherapy of Ida was on 2026-03-25.
    the finding disease progression absent about Ida is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the radiology report of 15 April describes a new enhancing lesion that meets the RANO criteria for progression".
    the Karnofsky performance score of Ida is 80.
    the finding full daily use expected about Ida is established, according to the treating practitioner.
    the TTFT device was delivered on 2026-04-20.
    rn expects answers [].
